NOTES
  * memory-one cube, F1, mean efficient share: computed 0.864859. facts_m1.md:1051 states 0.865 (agrees) and facts_m1.md:1059-1060 (the M1f README table, RM:97-103) 0.87, which is 0.864859 rounded twice (to 0.865, then 0.87); at two decimals it is 0.86.
  * binary memory one, replicate row: no per-replicate atom shares are available locally. wfdata.load('m1', run) returns pooled shares only; DiskM1WF/Data/mw1_e4.rep.tsv and mw2_e4.rep.tsv carry per replicate only pay, ef and ps1..ps4, the population's mean cooperation probability after each outcome (DiskM1WF/Cannon/mw/sf1.f:403-426), four marginals of sixteen shares. The w-files with each replicate's ten most abundant strategies (DiskM1WF/PROJECT.md:442) are not in the local tree. The binary paper states only a different criterion: at 59 (N = 100) and 11 (N = 1000) games the ten replicates fixed in different basins (some atom's between-replicate s.d. > 0.05; the binary paper [PR2026]; DiskM1WF/Data/bistable.tsv, 11 F1 and 59 F2 lines).
  * binary memory two, replicate row: 487 (F1) and 412 (F2) reproduce the binary paper [PR2026] and facts_ref.md:726; they come from the seeded re-runs f1_e4 / f2_e4, not from wfdata, and are exact per-replicate atom shares (the .rep files), not the rank-1 proxy of the .win files.
  * the leading atom of every space is its loader's; the raw argmax of the pooled shares gives the same leader at every game in all eight runs (rawdiff = F1 b1 0, F1 c1 0, F1 b2 0, F1 c2 0, F2 b1 0, F2 c1 0, F2 b2 0, F2 c2 0).

